    {
      "question": "Is 401(k) auto-enrollment mandatory?",
      "answer": "No, automatic enrollment is not mandatory for employees. Federal law requires covered employers to enroll eligible workers by default, but you always have the statutory right under 26 U.S.C. 414A to opt out of contributions entirely or select a different savings rate."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I opt out of automatic enrollment?",
      "answer": "Yes, you can opt out of automatic enrollment at any time. Your plan administrator must provide an automatic enrollment notice specifying the deadline and procedure for electing a 0% contribution rate before deductions begin."
    },
